WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.330
Look at an ordinary French menu.

2
00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:03.800
Couscous is on it.

3
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.750
Listen to French music: there is «raï»,

4
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:12.100
from Algeria. In 1998, France's
World Cup winners got a nickname:

5
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.690
«black-blanc-beur». One of those players,

6
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:18.380
Zinedine Zidane, is the
son of Algerian immigrants.

7
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.590
So how much does diversity
really change a country?

8
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:24.020
And can tolerance be learned?

9
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.860
In this mission, you'll build Mission D1,

10
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.940
a map of what the mix brings,

11
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.340
and read what the data
say about «la tolérance».

12
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.540
Then you'll climb Mission D2,

13
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.280
from «l'école» to «le travail»,

14
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.010
and argue: «une richesse ou un défi»?

15
00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.750
Your mission: explain how
diversity changes a country,

16
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.560
and whether tolerance can be taught.
